        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "12] On perusal of the record, it is found that, it is true that the sanction to prosecute the wife of the complainant PW-3 Anil Mishra was granted one day prior to the filing of the complaint, but its benefit cannot be granted to the appell"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "91e77b10338f4195ba0e2731c8a32d4a_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is also found that the complainant has supported the case of the prosecution that he had lodged a complaint Ex.P/2 in the Office of Lokayukt, and had also brought Rs.1,000/- (ten notes of Rs.100/- denomination)."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "723645e085404d7b809aeaa4db9590c9_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is also found that this witness PW-3 has stated that he had kept the amount in the pocket of the shirt of the appellant and after he was declared hostile in his cross-examination by the prosecution, he has feigned ignorance if the appell"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "263c9d7276d1463d9f6a17305d134fcc_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nApparently, there is nothing on record to suggest that the appellant's shirt's pocket was also washed,\nwhich could have substantiated the story of the defence that the amount was kept by the complainant in the shirt's pocket of the appella"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "484cff9350de4c7f82edfe86a612511b_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, despite the fact that he (the complainant Anil Mishra) has admitted that he was having a grudge against the appellant because a case was registered by the appellant against him, its benefit cannot be granted to the appellant."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ebb861c1bae24223b9949e2ffb172526_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n13] PW-2, H.C. Mishra, the Labour Officer, who is an independent NEUTRAL CITATION NO.\n2024:MPHC-IND:27708 CRA 1533-1999 witness, has also supported the case of the prosecution,\nregarding seizure of the currency notes from the pocket of the"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6d7c08f791284e2f8dcfc3235e585b55_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Although, PW-4 Subhash Rao S/o Shankar Rao, who is a witness to the procedure adopted has not supported the case of the prosecution, however, PW-5, Phoolsingh Raghuvanshi, SDO, has supported the case of the prosecution, who is also a witnes"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e5fff7bc8f544041b89ff588280334d2_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "] So far as the contention of the appellant that the complainant's wife's prosecution was already sanctioned on 09.10.1991, and there was no occasion for him to demand any amount from the complainant in this regard, this Court finds that it"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2c8527596961440c95e4f9d64ba89783_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n15] It is also found that in his accused statement under Section 313 of Cr.P.C., the appellant's defence is that he has been falsely implicated in the case only because he had taken sample from the appellant's premises, however, no evidenc"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "70a10bf798504ff7b53d462ce7237b1c_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n16] So far as Section 20 of the Act of 1988, is concerned, which provides for the presumption against the public servant, provides that if it is proved that a public servant accused of an offence has accepted or obtained for himself or for"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9742d2e020504afab5b4651354f73e03_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "So far as the discrepancy in Ex.P./3 is concerned, it is found that it has also been proved by PW-5,\nPhoolsingh Raghuvanshi, SDO, Lokayukt, Indore, who has stated that after recording the Dehati Nalishi, Ex.P/21, he had issued Ex.P/3 to the"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b65c714bd31d45d892988b195d93c2d9_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
